When a vertical-align length or percentage shifts an inline-level box,
Ladybird now sizes the line box from both edges of the shifted box,
with an atomic inline’s margins, and resolves a percentage against the
box’s own line-height. Blink does the same: InlineLayoutStateStack::
ApplyBaselineShift() moves the box’s FontHeight metrics by the shift,
and EndBoxState() unites them into the parent’s. So does WebKit, whose
LineBoxVerticalAligner::computeLineBoxLogicalHeight() takes each box’s
top and bottom from its shifted position. And so does Gecko, whose
nsLineLayout::VerticalAlignFrames() takes each frame’s contribution
from its shifted mBounds.
